Protest in the United Kingdom of Nottingham for the solidarity of our Kurdish brothers and sisters in the Rojava

‏January ٢٤, ٢٠٢٦

‏Said Saddik / Balen

‏We are gathered here today to stand in solidarity with our brothers and sisters in Rojava. We raise our voices alongside theirs to demand an immediate end to the massacres and injustices committed by the new Syrian regime under Ahmed al-Sharaa. I call him 'Nasharaa' (illegitimate), for if he followed any law or sanctity, he would not massacre innocent people. Therefore, he lacks both morality and legitimacy.
‏We have assembled at this demonstration to call upon the United Nations, the United States, Israel, the United Kingdom, the European Union, and all global powers and human rights advocates. We urge you: stop the terrorist regime in Syria. Force them to cease the killing of civilians, particularly the targeted violence against women and children.
‏In recent days, the world witnessed the brutal murder of a female Kurdish fighter (YPJ). They did not stop at killing her; they desecrated her body by throwing it from a high building. This was not just an insult to a deceased hero; it was a profound insult to every woman in the world. Following this, they cut the hair of another fallen female fighter—another act of degradation against womanhood.
‏I ask today: Where are the international human rights organizations? Where are the women's rights advocates? Why is there silence in the face of these atrocities? We must unite our voices to end this systemic oppression.
‏In ٢٠١٤, during the rise of ISIS, the Kurds were the most reliable allies of the United States and the international coalition. We were the most effective force on the ground, eliminating a global threat to protect both ourselves and the world.
‏Today, it is deeply painful to see that the US and its allies have allowed individuals with terrorist backgrounds to occupy positions of power and trust in Syria, effectively sidelining the Kurds. This is happening despite the immense sacrifice of the Kurdish people, who lost an estimated ١٥,٠٠٠ martyrs in the war against ISIS.
‏The United States and the international coalition must reassess their policies.
‏• Long live the Kurds!
‏• Long live the Resistance!
‏• Long live the Fighters!
‏• Victory to the rightful cause of our people!
‏• Shame upon the enemies of humanity and the terrorists